---
import BaseLayout from '../../layouts/BaseLayout.astro';
---

<BaseLayout
  title="Nolan's Workshop"
  description="Nolan's Workshop: woodworking projects, shop builds, jigs, tools, and lessons learned."
>
  <header class="page-header">
    <div class="shell">
      <p class="eyebrow">Woodworking</p>
      <h1>Nolan's Workshop</h1>
      <p class="lede">
        The woodworking side of the site: practical shop projects, jigs, furniture and builds, with the mistakes and tradeoffs left in.
      </p>
    </div>
  </header>

  <section class="section">
    <div class="shell prose">
      <h2>One site, a distinct workshop identity</h2>
      <p>
        Nolan's Workshop has its own name and physical wood brand. It lives here as a distinct section rather than forcing woodworking into an engineering portfolio or maintaining a second full website.
      </p>
      <p>
        Project writeups will be added selectively as useful build records are ready for public release.
      </p>
    </div>
  </section>
</BaseLayout>
